biti":[],"via":"","testo":"Borrowed from Middle Low German vut, from Old Saxon *fut, from Proto-West Germanic *futi (“vulva, uterus”)."},{"parola":"vracht","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"no","significato":"freight, cargo","termine_origine":"vracht","catena":[{"codice":"gml","nome":"Middle Low German","termine":"vracht","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"gmw-pro","nome":"Proto-West Germanic","termine":"*fra-","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"gmw-pro","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"From Middle Dutch vracht, from Middle Low German vracht, vrecht (“payment for cargo”), from Old Saxon frāht, frēht. Displaced the native Middle Dutch vrecht, both originally deriving from Proto-West Germanic *fra- + *aihti. Cognate with English freight and fraught."},{"parola":"zwoel","pos":"adj","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"prestito","incerta":"sì","motivo_incerta":"Probably","significato":"oppressive, muggy, sultry","termine_origine":"swōl","catena":[{"codice":"gml","nome":"Middle Low German","termine":"swōl","categoria":"prestito"},{"codice":"gmw-pro","nome":"Proto-West Germanic","termine":"*swelan","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"gmw-pro","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"From earlier swoel, probably from Middle Low German swōl, swūl (whence German Low German swool, German schwül), Old English swōl, swōliġ. Ultimately related to Proto-West Germanic *swelan (“to burn”). More at sweal."}]}